questions.question:
Match List-I (roster form) with List-II (set-builder form):
List-I
(a) {−2, 2}
(b) {0}
(c) {1, 2, 4, 8}
(d) {E, L, P, H, A, N, T}
List-II
(i) {x : x is an integer and x + 3 = 3}
(ii) {x : x is a letter of the word ELEPHANT}
(iii) {x : x is an integer and $x^2 = 4$}
(iv) {x : x is a natural number which divides 8}

How many of the following pairs consist of equal sets?
(i) The set of letters of LISTEN and the set of letters of SILENT
(ii) {x ∈ Z : $x^2 \le 1$} and {x ∈ R : $x^2 - x = 0$}
(iii) {x ∈ N : $x^2 = 9$} and {x ∈ Z : $x^2 = 9$}
(iv) {x : x is a prime number less than 10} and the set of prime factors of 210
(v) φ and {φ}

How many of the following pairs of sets are disjoint?
(i) {x : x is an even natural number} and {x : x is a prime number}
(ii) {x : x is an integer multiple of 4} and {x : x is an odd integer}
(iii) N and {x : x is a negative integer}
(iv) {x : x ∈ R, $x^2 = 1$} and {x : x ∈ Z, $x^3 = -1$}
(v) [0, 1) and [1, 2]

Let A = {x : x is an integer and $x^2 = 9$}. How many of the following sets are equal to A?
(i) {x : x ∈ R and $x^2 - 9 = 0$}
(ii) {x : x is an integral positive root of $x^2 - 9 = 0$}
(iii) {3, −3, 3, −3}
(iv) {x : x ∈ N and $x^2 = 9$}
(v) {x : x is an integer and $(x-3)(x+3)(x-3) = 0$}
(vi) {x : x is a rational number and $x^2 + 9 = 0$}

Let U = {1, 2, 3, ..., 10}, A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} and B = {4, 5, 6, 7}. Match List-I with List-II.
List-I:
(P) $A - B$
(Q) $A' \cap B$
(R) $(A \cup B)'$
(S) $(A \cap B)'$
List-II:
(1) {8, 9, 10}
(2) {1, 2, 3}
(3) {6, 7}
(4) {1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10}

Consider the sets
X = {x ∈ R : $x^2 = x$}
Y = {x ∈ R : $x^3 = x$}
Z = {x ∈ R : $x^4 = x^2$}
W = {x ∈ Z : |x| ≤ 1}
V = {x ∈ R : |x| = $x^2$}
How many of these sets are equal to the set {−1, 0, 1}?

Let A = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11} and B = {1, 3, 5, 7, 9}. How many of the following statements are correct?
(i) A − B = {2, 11}
(ii) B − A = {1, 9}
(iii) (A − B) ∪ (B − A) = A ∪ B
(iv) (A − B) ∪ (A ∩ B) = A
(v) $\sqrt{4}$ ∈ R − Q
